  "text": "Per-Comparison Error Rate Per-Comparison Error Rate The per-comparison error rate refers to the Type I error rate of any one significance test conducted as part of a series of significance tests. Thus, if 10 significance tests were each conducted at 0.05 significance level, then the per-comparison error rate would be 0.05. Compare with the familywise error rate .",
